    "title": "pandas.Index.join — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.join#\n\n- \n*final* Index.join(*other* ,*** ,*how='left'* ,*level=None* ,*return_indexers=False* ,*sort=False* )[source]#\n- Compute join_index and indexers to conform data structures to the new index. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **other** Index\n    - **how** {‘left’, ‘right’, ‘inner’, ‘outer’}\n    - **level** int or level name, default None\n    - **return_indexers** bool, default False\n    - **sort** bool, default False\n    - Sort the join keys lexicographically in the result Index. If False, the order of the join keys depends on the join type (how keyword).\n  - Returns:\n    - join_index, (left_indexer, right_indexer)\n Examples >>> idx1 = pd.Index([1, 2, 3]) >>> idx2 = pd.Index([4, 5, 6]) >>> idx1.join(idx2, how='outer') Index([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], dtype='int64')",
    "markdown_length": 779,
